                                    </p>
                                    <div class="q-a">
                                        <h3>What is a Studmale and what does he needs?</h3>
                                        <p class="f-20 my-4">
                                            A stud refers to a male cat that is retained for breeding purposes. He possesses desirable physical and behavioural traits that breeders wish to pass on to the next generation of their kittens.
                                            The term “stud” highlights the cat’s role in breeding, as he is used to provide litters. Typically, a stud is selected based on various things including:
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <p class="f-20">
                                        <ul class="f-20" style="list-style-type: disc; line-height: 32px;">
                                            <li class="my-2"><strong style="color: #ff344f;">Physical Attributes:</strong> A stud male should ideally represent the best physical qualities of his breed. This includes size of the cat and his offspring, coat quality and looks, physical characteristics.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2"><strong style="color: #ff344f;">Health:</strong> It’s essential that a stud male is free from genetic disorders or diseases that can be passed to his offspring. Regular health checks like FIV/FeLV tests and certain health clearances might be mandatory in many formal breeding settings. Some breeds ask specific checks like HCM and PKD for example. You can ask your association what kind of tests are required for your breed.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2"><strong style="color: #ff344f;">Temperament:</strong> A good stud male should also possess a temperament that is typical and desirable for the breed. This ensures that not just physical but also behavioral traits are passed on to his next generation. It's important to ask and describe what type of cat fit in your breeding program.</li>
                                            <li class="my-2"><strong style="color: #ff344f;">Breeding Success:</strong> Past success in previous litters that are healthy, of good size, and that adhere closely to breed standards can also be a factor in an cat desirability as a stud.</li>
                                        </ul>
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
